# Backend

## Structure

- Routes: `backend/app/api/` (`articles`, `clusters`, `bias`, `rumors`) mounted in `app/api/__init__.py`
- Models: `app/models/` (`article`, `cluster`, `source`); Pydantic: `app/schemas/`
- Business logic: `app/services/` (`rss_parser`, `ai_client`) — keep route handlers thin
- Seed data: `app/data/bd_sources_seed.py`
- Config: `app/core/config.py` (`Settings`, prefix `/api/v1`)
- DB: `app/core/database.py`; tables created on startup in `app/main.py` lifespan
- Health: `GET /health` (outside API prefix)

## API surface

- `GET /api/v1/articles`, `/clusters`, `/clusters/{slug}`, `/bias`, `/rumors`
- OpenAPI: `/docs` when server is running

## Patterns

- Use **async** endpoints and DB/HTTP for I/O-bound work
- Add new resources as a router module + schema + model; register on `api_router`
- AI calls go through `AIClient`; respect `settings.ai_provider` and optional API keys
- Planned jobs: RSS ingest via `rss_parser`; cluster summaries via `ai_client.summarize_cluster`

## Example route shape

```python
@router.get("", response_model=ArticleListResponse)
async def list_articles(session: AsyncSession = Depends(get_session), limit: int = 12) -> ArticleListResponse:
    ...
```
